---
components: ["Loading"]
description: Loading indicators display a full-screen or inline spinner, ideal for showing progress during page loads or data fetching.
---

<script>
  import { Loading } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Display a loading indicator with a semi-transparent overlay that covers the entire viewport. While active, the overlay holds keyboard focus. Focus returns to the previous element when loading stops.

<FileSource src="/framed/Loading/Loading" />

## No overlay

Show a loading indicator without the overlay, allowing interaction with the underlying content.

<Loading withOverlay={false} />

## Small

Display a more compact loading indicator.

<Loading withOverlay={false} small />

## Description

Customize the text announced to screen readers by setting `description`. Defaults to `"loading"`.

<Loading description="Loading metrics..." withOverlay={false} />

## Delay

Set `delay` to wait a number of milliseconds after `active` becomes `true` before rendering the spinner. Requests that finish within the delay never show a spinner, avoiding a flash of loading state for fast responses.

<FileSource src="/framed/Loading/LoadingDelay" />

## Transition

The spinner and its overlay appear and disappear at once by default. Set `transition` to fade them as the `{#if}` that holds them, or `delay`, shows and removes them. `true` uses Carbon's fade (`moderate02`, 240 ms), fade parameters such as `{ duration: "slow01" }` customize it, and `{ fn }` swaps in another [transition](/motion#transitions). Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` they still appear and disappear at once.

The leaving overlay becomes inert, so it takes no clicks, and focus returns to where it was once the fade ends. `Loading` forwards `introstart`, `introend`, `outrostart`, and `outroend`.

<FileSource src="/framed/Loading/LoadingTransition" />

## Stop state

Set `active` to `false` to play the spinner's end-of-loading animation and mark it inactive for screen readers (`aria-live="off"`). Useful when transitioning out of a loading state before removing the component.

<Loading active={false} withOverlay={false} />
